    "created_at": "2020-01-03T23:44:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-03T23:45:16Z",
    "body": "The `requestDevice` method intentionally returns a `sequence<HIDDevice>` to account for the fact that a single USB device (for example) may include multiple USB functions all implementing the USB HID specification. Logically these are a single device but each has its own HID report descriptor and set of supported reports. This specification needs some way of indicating to page that the user has selected this kind of composite device.\r\n\r\nMy suggestion is to add an additional layer of indirection between `HIDDevice` (which is a single physical device) and `HIDCollectionInfo` called something like `HIDInterface`. A single `HIDDevice` could have multiple `HIDInterface`s but they all share common device properties such as USB vendor and product IDs and strings.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
